{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JfEFqsLLmWaZdnTeDe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your background makes a strong case for this job. Before I write it, a few questions. Each answer would change what the letter says:\n\n1. **What's the practice called, and who should the letter go to?** If the posting names a hiring contact, I'll address the letter to them. Otherwise I'll use a general greeting.\n2. **Did you supervise the clinic staff yourself?** If so, roughly how many people reported to you? The posting says this role supervises 9, so direct management experience would be one of your strongest points.\n3. **How much do you want to say about the gap?** My suggestion is one short, plain sentence: you left to care for your mother full-time, and that chapter has ended. Then the letter moves straight to what you did during those years. Tell me if you'd rather say more, or less.\n4. **Have you started learning Dentrix, or would you be willing to before you start?** Watching their free tutorials or asking about a trial would let me write \"I've begun learning Dentrix\" instead of just \"I've used similar software.\" That makes the gap look smaller.\n5. **Do you have a connection to this practice or to local patients?** For example, you might be a patient there or have lived in town a long time. A single line about it makes a letter to a small local practice feel less generic.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, just say so. I'll write around anything you leave out rather than guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":9530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pa